# The first hour, felt through the real keys on a new seed-1 game (M1.5):
# wake and read the goal, a worker on its round seen across the fields,
# gather, lay a fire, set charcoal going and walk off while it cooks, a pick
# before noon, the first meeting won by reading the runner's tell and
# striking its working side, a slide round a tree, and something put down and
# taken back. tours/wild.tour is the same first minutes with nothing scripted.
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=420 tools/tour.sh tours/feel.tour --give=driftwood:6,scrap:1
# (--give brings the tip's plate and tops the wood up, as core_loop does.)
#
# Wake: the guide says what to want first.
wait 2.4
shot 01-wake-the-goal
# Up in the coast fields in the first minute: a worker crosses on its round,
# well off, and goes by. (No hunter comes out this early: the first meeting
# waits a minute or so into the game.)
at 130,370
wait 1.0
wait 6
shot 01b-a-worker-on-its-round
wait 5
shot 01c-still-on-its-round
# The scripted gathering is not a random fight: nothing comes until the fields again.
coast calm
# Driftwood on the strand below the village.
near driftwood
walk 0,0 0.05
press use 0.1
await took 3
wait 0.3
shot 02-gathered
near driftwood,wrack
walk 0,0 0.05
press use 0.1
await took 3
# A loose stone off each of two boulders.
near boulder,stone ore
walk 0,0 0.05
press use 0.1
await took 6
near boulder,stone ore
walk 0,0 0.05
press use 0.1
await took 6
# Open ground west of the village: the first press asks, the second lays the fire.
at 188.5,428.5
walk -1,0 0.08
press use 0.1
wait 0.3
press use 0.1
await made 4
wait 0.5
shot 03-fire-laid
# Charcoal is set going on the fire, and a haft whittled while it starts.
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose charcoal
tap use
wait 0.4
choose haft
tap use
await made 3
tap pause
wait 0.4
shot 04-charcoal-on-the-fire
# Walk off along the strand while it cooks: the clock runs, the fire works.
walk 1,1 2.5
wait 1.0
shot 05-walking-while-it-cooks
# Back at the fire when it is done: it comes off into the creel.
at 188.5,428.5
walk -1,0 0.05
await made 60
wait 0.4
shot 06-charcoal-taken
# The pick, set going the same way; waited out by the fire.
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose pick_made
tap use
wait 0.3
tap pause
await made 70
wait 0.4
shot 07-a-pick-before-noon
tap inventory
wait 0.6
shot 08-carrying-the-pick
tap inventory
wait 0.4
# Out to the coast fields, with the knife back in hand for the meeting. The
# coast is asked for by NAME (GenPlaces), not by a coordinate: worldgen has
# moved this island twice now, and a pinned tile quietly stops being the open
# fields a machine walks its round across.
place coast
zoom 15
wait 1.0
coast wild
# The game is past its first minute: the first meeting comes out, a lone
# runner a fair walk off, and makes for the player once it has seen them.
zoom 11
await tell 30
shot 11-runner-tell
# Read the tell: out of its bite by going round its flank while it is committed,
# to its back, where the drive is, and strike as it stands spent.
walkto part 1.3
shot 12-round-to-its-back
tap swing
try 8
await hit 1.0
end
wait 0.05
shot 13-struck-its-working-side
# Stalled by the blow, it takes a second.
tap swing
wait 0.6
# Each bite after the same way: the tell, round it, strike, strike.
try 10
await tell 8
walkto part 1.3
tap swing
await hit 1.0
end
tap swing
wait 0.6
try 10
await tell 8
walkto part 1.3
tap swing
await killed 1.0
end
wait 0.6
shot 14-the-runner-down
# Sliding: a run held north-east into a broadleaf goes round its trunk.
coast calm
zoom 9
at 119.64,358.00
wait 0.6
shot 15-before-the-tree
walk 1,0 1.4 run
wait 0.2
shot 16-slid-round-the-tree
# Something put down: hold X, and the knife in hand is left on a heap (the
# pick is carried, so it is not the only blade). E takes it back.
press drop 0.8
wait 0.3
shot 17-put-down
press use 0.1
await took 2
wait 0.3
shot 18-taken-back
